Usages:
  mutable_impl_pattern: |
    Each read-only, property-heavy interface in this cell (SManga, SChapter) ships with a
    companion *Impl class that is a plain mutable holder of the same properties, created via
    the interface's own create() factory. External source implementations are free to
    implement the interface directly instead of using the provided Impl.

Annotations: |
  This is the data model of the cross-boundary contract between the host app and a Source/
  CatalogueSource implementation (in-repo LocalSource, or an out-of-process extension APK).
  Every type here is a plain data holder with no dependency on any other cell in this forest;
  it is the lowest layer of the source-facing surface.

  Use `mutable_impl_pattern` for SManga/SChapter.

---

"SManga()":
  location: SManga.kt
  annotations: |
    Mutable manga metadata as produced by a source, before it is merged into the domain Manga
    entity (a separate cell) by the app.

    Algorithm:
    1. getGenres() splits the flat, comma-separated genre string into a trimmed, deduplicated
       list, or returns null when genre is blank
    2. copy() builds a new instance via create() and copies every property across

    Use `mutable_impl_pattern` for how a concrete instance is obtained (create() /
    `SMangaImpl`).
  properties:
    "url -> String": |
      Source-specific identifier/path for this manga.
    "title -> String": |
      Manga title as provided by the source.
    "thumbnail_url -> String?": |
      Cover image URL, or null if the source has none.
    "artist -> String?": |
      Artist name, or null if unknown.
    "author -> String?": |
      Author name, or null if unknown.
    "status -> Int": |
      Publication status; one of the UNKNOWN/ONGOING/COMPLETED/LICENSED/
      PUBLISHING_FINISHED/CANCELLED/ON_HIATUS constants declared on this type.
    "description -> String?": |
      Synopsis text, or null if the source has none.
    "genre -> String?": |
      Flat, comma-separated genre list as provided by the source; use getGenres() to parse it.
    "update_strategy -> UpdateStrategy": |
      How the library-update job should treat this manga going forward; see `UpdateStrategy`.
    "initialized -> Boolean": |
      Whether this manga's metadata has been fetched from the source at least once.
    "memo -> JsonObject": |
      Source-specific extra metadata, opaque to the app.

"SChapter()":
  location: SChapter.kt
  annotations: |
    Mutable chapter metadata as produced by a source, before it is merged into the domain
    Chapter entity (a separate cell) by the app.

    Algorithm:
    1. copyFrom(other) overwrites every source-supplied property from other

    Use `mutable_impl_pattern` for how a concrete instance is obtained (create() /
    `SChapterImpl`).
  properties:
    "url -> String": |
      Source-specific identifier/path for this chapter.
    "name -> String": |
      Chapter title as provided by the source.
    "chapter_number -> Float": |
      Parsed chapter number, or a negative value if unrecognized.
    "scanlator -> String?": |
      Scanlation group name, or null if not provided.
    "date_upload -> Long": |
      Epoch millis the chapter was uploaded on the source.
    "memo -> JsonObject": |
      Source-specific extra metadata, opaque to the app.
  methods:
    "copyFrom(other: SChapter)": |
      Overwrite name, url, date_upload, chapter_number, scanlator, and memo from
      other.

"SManga::SMangaImpl()":
  location: SMangaImpl.kt
  annotations: |
    Concrete, mutable, lateinit-backed implementation of SManga returned by SManga.create().
    Every property defaults to an empty/neutral value until a source fills it in.

"SChapter::SChapterImpl()":
  location: SChapterImpl.kt
  annotations: |
    Concrete, mutable, lateinit-backed implementation of SChapter returned by
    SChapter.create().

"MangasPage(mangas: List<SManga>, hasNextPage: Boolean)":
  location: MangasPage.kt
  annotations: |
    One page of a paginated manga listing (popular/latest/search) returned by a source.

    mangas: the page's manga results, using SManga
    `hasNextPage`: whether the source has at least one more page after this one

"Page(index: Int, url: String, imageUrl: String?)":
  location: Page.kt
  annotations: |
    One page image of a chapter, plus its own download/decoding progress state, tracked as a
    small state machine so the reader UI can subscribe to per-page progress.

    `index`: zero-based position within the chapter; number (index + 1) is the 1-based
    label shown to the user
    url: page identifier/URL as provided by the source; may be empty if `imageUrl` is already
    known
    `imageUrl`: direct image URL once resolved, or null before resolution

    Algorithm:
    1. status moves through State.Queue -> State.LoadPage -> State.DownloadImage ->
       State.Ready, or to State.Error on failure
    2. update(bytesRead, contentLength, done) recomputes progress (0-100) from the
       downloaded byte count whenever a source reports incremental download progress
  properties:
    "number -> Int": |
      1-based display index, index + 1.
    "status -> State": |
      Current stage in the page's fetch/decode lifecycle.
    "progress -> Int": |
      0-100 download completion percentage; -1 when the total size is unknown.
  methods:
    "update(bytesRead: Long, contentLength: Long, done: Boolean)": |
      Recompute progress from `bytesRead`/`contentLength`; called by the underlying HTTP
      client as bytes arrive.

"FilterList(list: List<Filter<Any>>)":
  location: FilterList.kt
  annotations: |
    An ordered, source-defined list of search filters, passed back to
    getSearchManga/fetchSearchManga unchanged from what getFilterList() returned (after the
    user edits filter state in place).

"Filter(name: String, state: T)":
  location: Filter.kt
  annotations: |
    Base type for one configurable search filter exposed by a source. Concrete filter kinds are
    nested subclasses: Header and Separator (non-interactive, Any state), Select
    (single choice from values, Int index state), Text (free-text `String` state),
    CheckBox (Boolean state), TriState (ignore/include/exclude Int state, via
    isIgnored()/isIncluded()/isExcluded()), Group (a named sub-list of filters, List<V>
    state), and Sort (choice of one of values plus ascending/descending, via the nested
    Selection data class).

    name: filter's display label
    `state`: filter's current value, whose type and meaning depend on the concrete filter kind

"UpdateStrategy()":
  location: UpdateStrategy.kt
  annotations: |
    How the library-update background job should treat a manga going forward: ALWAYS_UPDATE
    (check for new chapters every run) or ONLY_FETCH_ONCE (skip on subsequent runs, for series
    already known to be finished with a single chapter).

"SMangaUpdate(manga: SManga, chapters: List<SChapter>)":
  location: SMangaUpdate.kt
  annotations: |
    Result of Source.getMangaUpdate: the manga's own metadata (unchanged from the input if
    fetchDetails was false) plus the resolved chapter list (unchanged from the input if
    fetchChapters was false).

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  The data model half of the source-api extension contract: the mutable manga/chapter shapes a
  Source implementation reads and writes, plus pagination, filters, and per-page download
  state. Consumed by the Source/CatalogueSource contract cell and, one level further out, by
  the domain Manga model.
